            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The offer of Negative Pressure Wound Therapy (NPWT) has considerably increased these last years. Nowadays, one can choose between different tools such as motorised systems - or not - like pumps; devices which are particularly portables; automated therapies allowing regular instillations; or finally systems adapted to specific indications like &quot;open abdominal wounds&quot;. This diversity of devices implies more than ever that prescriptions from the medical doctor be detailed and a good trackability of the nursing follow-up.</AbstractText>
